              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner (Attorney General John D. Ashcroft), according to Petitioner (Attorney General John D. Ashcroft), the Child Online Protection Act (COPA) was presented as a response to pervasive commercial Internet pornography that causes substantial physical and psychological damage to children."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6b8d232e818e-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 12,
              "start": 12
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioner argues that millions of children are exposed to pornographic material online, with about 11\u202fmillion children visiting such sites each week and 70\u202fpercent of 15\u2011 to 17\u2011year\u2011olds doing so inadvertently."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondents",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 27,
              "start": 26
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0007"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 33
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Respondents contend that the statute\u2019s protection for minors is narrower than that for adults and that it imposes a greater burden on speech."
      }
    ],
